// TEST: Number Glued To Name (rejects)
// ERROR: BL0003 @ 8:9-8:11
// ERROR-CONTAINS: no implicit multiplication, so write `2 * x`
// `2x` used to lex as the literal 2 followed by the name x, which the parser
// then split into `let b = 2` plus a printed bare `x`. A number glued to a
// name is now one malformed literal, reported over its whole span.
let x = 3.0
let b = 2x
